# Documentation Editing Rules

## Document-Driven Development
This project follows strict DDD. Documentation is the source of truth.

## When Editing Documentation
1. **Cross-reference**: If your change affects other docs, update them too
2. **Keep consistent**: Terminology must match across all docs
3. **Update PROGRESS.md**: After any task completion, update the checkboxes and changelog
4. **ADR format**: New architectural decisions go in DECISIONS.md using the established format:
   ```markdown
   ### ADR-NNN: Title
   - **Status**: Accepted
   - **Context**: Why this decision was needed
   - **Decision**: What we decided
   - **Consequences**: Tradeoffs and impacts
   ```

## Cross-Reference Map
When you change one doc, check if these related docs need updates:

| If you change... | Also check... |
|-----------------|---------------|
| ARCHITECTURE.md | CONTEXT.md (design rules), relevant phase doc, DECISIONS.md (ADRs) |
| phases/phase-{n}.md | PROGRESS.md (task list matches), TRACEABILITY.md (file mappings) |
| API_SPEC.md | relevant phase doc (route tasks), ARCHITECTURE.md (protocol) |
| SECURITY.md | AGENTS.md (security section), relevant phase doc |
| LLM_STRATEGY.md | ARCHITECTURE.md (parsing pipeline), relevant phase doc |
| DECISIONS.md | CONTEXT.md (design rules), relevant technical doc |
| PROGRESS.md | TRACEABILITY.md (if marking task complete) |
| TRACEABILITY.md | No cascading updates — this is the audit trail |

## PROGRESS.md Update Format
```markdown
### Changelog
- YYYY-MM-DD: Brief description of what was done
```

Checkbox format:
- `⬜` = Not started
- `🔄` = In progress
- `✅` = Complete

## NEVER
- Never remove documentation without moving the content elsewhere
- Never change an ADR status from "Accepted" to anything without a new superseding ADR
- Never edit docs without reading the current content first
- Never add a task to a phase doc without a corresponding entry in PROGRESS.md
